Deployment, Hosting, Backup & Monitoring
Cloud Infrastructure: Use a major cloud provider (AWS/GCP/Azure) with containerized microservices (e.g. Docker + Kubernetes or serverless functions). Key services: Web frontend, API backend (e.g. Node/Java/.NET), relational database (PostgreSQL or SQL Server), file storage (S3-compatible) for documents.
Redundancy & Scaling: Deploy across multiple availability zones. Use managed services for DB with read replicas. Auto-scale web/API tiers based on CPU/memory. Use a global CDN for static assets and portal delivery.
Continuous Delivery: CI/CD pipeline for builds and deployments; automated testing (unit/integration) and blue/green deployment. Alma mentions iterative releases every 2 weeks
. We’ll adopt a similar agile cadence for updates.
Backups & DR: Daily database backups retained (e.g. 30 days). Long-term backups (weekly/monthly) for compliance retention (years). Off-site replication for disaster recovery. Define RPO/RTO (e.g. RPO=4 hours, RTO=2 hours) and test drills.
Logging & Monitoring:
Application Monitoring: Instrument APIs with Prometheus/Grafana for real-time metrics (error rates, latency, throughput).
Uptime Monitoring: External health checks (Pingdom/New Relic) to verify service endpoints are reachable (target 99.9%). Alma guarantees “cloud-native” high availability
.
Logging: Central log aggregation (ELK/Stackdriver) for audits and troubleshooting. Security logs for all user actions.
Alerts: Set thresholds (e.g. CPU > 80%, error rate spikes) to trigger alerts to on-call devops.
Support Environments: Separate development, staging, and production environments. Data masking in non-prod.
Metrics, KPIs & Success Criteria
To measure success and guide decisions, the following metrics should be tracked:

System Performance: API response times (p90 < 1s), page load times. Uptime percentage (aim ≥ 99.9% monthly). SLA compliance (time to restore, etc.).
Adoption & Usage: Percentage of teachers actively using gradebook/attendance features; daily/monthly active users (by role); number of parent/students logging in. Target high adoption (e.g. ≥ 80% of teachers using core modules).
Data Quality: Rate of incomplete records (e.g. % of students without contact info).
Operational Efficiency: Time saved vs. previous solution (e.g. average time to take attendance or produce a report). Can be measured in user surveys post-implementation.
Engagement: Volume of messages sent through system (e.g. number of parent messages).
Financial Metrics: Fees collected on time, reduction in late payments.
Customer Satisfaction: Survey-based NPS from staff and parents, support ticket resolution time.
Project Metrics: Implementation milestones met (on-time delivery of MVP features).
